-- A collection `get` result is a shared alias to storage in the receiver's allocation. A mutable
-- slot that stores the alias cannot be passed by `~` for mutation while the immutable `rows`
-- binding still owns that storage. The catch fallback stores a fresh collection, but the joined
-- slot still aliases `rows` on the success path.
mutate_param |rows {{I32}}|:
    slot ~{I32} = {0}
    ~slot = rows.get(0) catch:
        then {7}
    ;
    ~slot.push(4)
;
mutate_param({{9}})
